### Page 1 of 1

```text
1
RESOLUTION NO. ________

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION EXPRESSING THE CITY OF CHEYENNE’S DESIRE
AND COMMITMENT TO FACILITATING COMMERCIAL PASSENGER
AIR SERVICE AT THE CHEYENNE REGIONAL AIRPORT BOTH NOW
AND IN THE FUTURE.”

WHEREAS, the Economically Needed Diversity Options for Wyoming Executive
Council (“ENDOW”) was charged with charting a new course for Wyoming’s economy;

WHEREAS, ENDOW identified barriers to economic growth, including insufficient
infrastructure to support our present and future economies;

WHEREAS, ENDOW recommended improving and expanding Wyoming’s commercial
passenger air service as a critical element in reducing barriers to economic growth;

WHEREAS, in support of that goal, a new airport terminal is already being constructed at
the Cheyenne Regional Airport and is financially supported by local, state, and federal agencies;

WHEREAS, constructing the terminal is only one part of facilitating commercial
passenger air service—the terminal also requires an air carrier to service it;

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne (“City”) expresses its commitment to financially
supporting commercial passenger air service at that facility to enable it to serve the City; and

WHEREAS, the City also understands that other local governmental and public-sector
entities have also expressed interest in supporting air service at the Cheyenne Regional Airport;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the City is (1) willing to expend up to Six Hundred
Thousand Dollars ($600,000.00) before the conclusion of FY2019 to support commercial
passenger air service at the Cheyenne Regional Airport both now and in the future; and (2) urges
future City leaders to support and invest in on-going, consistent, reliable local air service.

PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED this ____ day of ___________, 2018.

____________________________
Marian J. Orr, Mayor

(Seal)

ATTEST:

____________________________
Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk
By BJR as to form only at 10:55 am, May 09, 2018
```
